## 33. Known Limits and Current Gaps

The current implementation is functional but not yet multi-host.

Known limits:

- VS Code is the only implemented detection host; JetBrains, Neovim, and a standalone CLI ingest are not yet built.
- The provider-agnostic core is defined at the schema/types level, but capture, search, and UI still live inside the VS Code host and backend service layers.
- External plugin loading is not implemented; adapters are internal modules registered in code.
- Manual import provenance is not implemented yet.
- HTTPS CONNECT traffic is tunnel-only unless a separate trusted interception sidecar is added.
- Backend lineage currently creates initial Neo4j lineage versions but does not yet perform full multi-version relationship evolution on ingest.
- Backend tests focus on config/security/insights; backend ingest/search/Neo4j integration tests are not broad yet.
- All project docs now live in `docs/` (architecture.md, repo-map.md, lightweight-adapters.md, native-backend.md, shipping-modes.md, CHANGELOG.md, SUPPORT.md, SHIP_PRODUCTS_COMMANDS.md).
- Deploy compose bundles are now under `deploy/` rather than the root.
- Release artifacts are under `releases/` (solo .vsix, team .zip, enterprise .zip).

